  "fibres": [],
  "measures": [],
  "notes": "Second-harmonic generation in periodically poled crystals. Top: 2 W at 1560 nm (an erbium fibre amplifier’s output, collimated to 1 mm) focused into 50 mm of MgO:PPLN, doubled to 780 nm (the rubidium line, the usual way to reach it from telecom lasers). Bottom: 1 W at 1064 nm into 20 mm of PPKTP, doubled to 532 nm. Each crystal’s period is the best for its beam at the temperature set; a short-pass filter passes the harmonic to a photodiode. Select a crystal to read the efficiency (%/W), the phase matching and the focusing against Boyd and Kleinman’s optimum, and to see the harmonic against temperature. Press Play on the PPLN’s temperature sweep: a degree off and the harmonic is gone. Raise the pump power and watch the conversion saturate as the fundamental is used up; move the crystal off the focus, or change the lens, and the efficiency falls.",
  "ui": {
    "sel": "xA",
    "pins": [],
    "views": {}
  }
